  "context": "Customer wants to know which DR strategy fits their application backend. Confirmed facts from the customer: (1) RPO 15 minutes and RTO 1 hour required for customer and purchase data (this lives in dr-demo-mysql) if the eu-central-1 Region fails. (2) dr-demo-valkey is a cache that can be fully rebuilt from the database — treat it as rebuildable, so it does NOT need cross-Region replication, but still check its in-Region redundancy/snapshot setup for the service-failure and AZ-failure scenarios. (3) dr-demo-players is part of the application backend (likely the compute/app tier) — identify what it actually is and check its in-Region redundancy, and whether images/AMIs/IaC exist that could redeploy it elsewhere. No recovery Region has been chosen yet by the customer — check for cross-Region artifacts (snapshots, replicas, AMI/image copies, secrets, KMS keys) in eu-west-1 as a candidate EU-based recovery Region, and note if anything exists there already; also check what IaC/pipeline exists that could deploy this workload to another Region.",
  "resources": ["dr-demo-mysql", "dr-demo-valkey", "dr-demo-players", "eu-central-1", "eu-west-1 (candidate recovery Region, to check only)"],
  "timeframe": "current state as of now (point-in-time configuration check, not a historical time range)",
  "criteria": "For dr-demo-mysql: MultiAZ, BackupRetentionPeriod, ReadReplicaDBInstanceIdentifiers, DeletionProtection, StorageEncrypted, cross-Region read replicas or Aurora Global Database, automated backup replication, snapshots in eu-west-1. For dr-demo-valkey: DescribeReplicationGroups (AutomaticFailover, MultiAZ, member count, SnapshotRetentionLimit, GlobalReplicationGroupInfo, node type/family), DescribeSnapshots. For dr-demo-players: identify resource type first, then AZ/task/instance spread, single point of failure or not, where its deployable artifact (AMI/container image/code) lives and whether it exists or could exist in eu-west-1, entry/routing (load balancer) in front of it and its AZ spread. Shared dependencies: VPC/network, Secrets Manager secret replica Regions, KMS key Region(s), certificates, IaC/CloudFormation stack(s) for this workload and whether they could deploy to eu-west-1. Flag anything denied or not checked explicitly."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Gather DR readiness data for dr-demo workload (RDS MySQL, ElastiCache Valkey, app layer) in eu-central-1."}], "created_at": null}

